    description: "FOUND 2026-08-16 while resolving the Tauros. FIXED 2026-08-21 (v1.65), after the author confirmed the loadout line was exactly what it looked like — \"'The Sister Superior is equipped with: Boltgun; Frag grenades; Krak grenades.' is already on the Datasheet. Probably a parsing error?\" — which sent this back for a real fix instead of staying filed. CAUSE, found by live-testing the promotion: `computeWeaponGroups` derives which base model a promotion came from as \"whatever sits right before the variant in the displayed model list\" — correct when the base group has more than one model and keeps its own row (9 Traitor Guardsmen next to the promoted Sergeant), wrong when the base group has exactly one model and its row gets REPLACED outright by the promotion (Sister Superior → Veteran Superior, nothing named \"Sister Superior\" left to sit next to). With her row gone, \"whatever sits right before\" the Veteran Superior was Sister Novitiate instead — so the fold-the-promoted-model's-weapons-in step landed on the Novitiates, reading 10x Auto pistol/Autogun/Frag grenade for a 9-model squad. FIX: derive the promoted base the same way points.ts already prices it — `getPromotedModel`, which reads the option group's own header text (\"The Sister Superior may be upgraded to...\") instead of guessing from position. Verified live: Sister Novitiate now reads 9x correctly, and Sister Superior's own row now shows 1x Boltgun (previously no count at all). Same fix likely also correct for Dominion Squad, Retributor Squad and Battle Sisters Squad, which share the identical Sister Superior → Veteran Superior shape — checked that Chaos Space Marines' Champion → Aspiring Champion promotion (a different code path, since the Champion's loadout is identical to the squad's) was already correct and stayed correct.",
