    description: 'CLOSED 2026-06-26 via a proper exhaustive pass: read every one of the 36 `advisor: true` units\' OWN option_group header / ability text (not just grepping the literal "Advisor:" string) and found two more bug shapes beyond the original 3 missing-flag cases. (1) FALSE POSITIVES — `advisor: true` with zero supporting ratio text anywhere: Custodian Wardens (Adeptus Custodes) and Platoon Command Squad (Imperial Guard, whose actual mechanic is the unrelated ki-45b Platoon-linking system) — both flipped to `advisor: false`. (2) WRONG ANCHOR — `advisor: true` correctly present, but the unit\'s own text ratios against something OTHER than HQ count, so the hardcoded HQ-count anchor in `advisorExemptIds` was silently mis-crediting it: T\'au Sub-Commander (ratio vs Commander+Ethereal, not any HQ), T\'au Ethereal Guard (ratio vs Ethereal specifically), T\'au Kroot Lone-Spear/Krootox Riders/Krootox Rampagers (all 3 ratio vs Kroot Carnivores — Riders/Rampagers\' header text also said "ELITE slot" despite being Heavy Support/Fast Attack themselves, a copy-paste artifact from Lone-Spear\'s text, corrected to match each unit\'s own slot). All 5 wrong-anchor units flipped to `advisor: false` and given dedicated `computeXFreeSlots` functions with the correct anchor, same pattern as the Commissar fix.',
